      "answer": "Here is the **Poison** condition as defined in the Gloomhaven (2nd Edition) rulebook and FAQ:\n\n---\n\n## Poison — Gloomhaven (2nd Edition)\n\n> **Poison:** All attacks targeting the figure gain \"+1 [curse star].\" Poison is removed when the figure is healed but, unlike wound, poison prevents the heal from increasing the figure's current hit point value.\n\n*(Rulebook, passage 114)*\n\n### Key points\n\n- **Attack penalty on the poisoned figure:** Every attack targeting a *Poisoned* figure gets +1 to its attack modifier draw (the curse-star effect, meaning one extra negative card is drawn).\n- **Removal:** *Poison* is removed when the figure is targeted by a *Heal* ability — even if the heal does nothing else useful.\n- **Heal interaction:** A single heal can remove both *Wound* and *Poison* at the same time. However, if *Poison* is present, **the hit point increase from that heal is prevented entirely.** *(Rulebook, passage 118)*\n- **Not stackable:** You cannot stack multiple instances of *Poison* on the same figure. If an attack would apply *Poison* more than once, only one token is placed. *(FAQ, passage 29)*\n- **Objectives are immune:** Objectives cannot gain *Poison* or any other condition. *(FAQ, passage 71)*",
